+  The three policy-fed capabilities are published on every pass. Since
+  R12-RES-8026 three dependency rows the cell measures itself are published
+  beside them — `feed`, `venue_session` and `clock` — **each only once the
+  cell has observed it** (`DegradationState::observed`, not `freshness`):
+  absent before any venue has been heard or any venue time measured, and
+  absent for `venue_session` on a cell built without venue health, because an
+  unobserved row's `unavailable` is a default, not a measurement. So the
+  `capability` label takes at most six values per cell. `ingestion` and
+  `counterfactual_scoring` remain deliberately absent: the cell never measures
+  either as a capability, and ingestion's envelope is the per-book
+  `stale_book` gate, stated as a `PerBook` row of the cell's
+  `qip_edge::degradation::DegradationEnvelope` and refused at assembly if
+  omitted. `ledger` is the halt gauge's `journal` source and `fabric` is
+  derived from the policy-fed rows, so neither is charted here twice. Locate
+  the recording site with
+  `grep -n 'state.observed(capability)' backend/crates/edge/qip-edge/src/telemetry.rs`.
 - `qip_edge_policy_sequence` — the payload the cell has *applied*, for
   correlation against what the centre believes it published.
 - `qip_edge_region_share_bound` and `qip_edge_region_share_applied_total{outcome}`
